<title>BANGLADESH: Cypriot tanker detained in Bangladesh.</title>
<headline>Cypriot tanker detained in Bangladesh.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG, Bangladesh 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cypriot-flagged tanker Saraband has been detained under a court order after the Bangladesh state-owned oil company sought compensation worth 113.7 million taka ($2.7 million) for late arrival, port officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>They said the admiralty bench of Bangladesh High Court had &quot;attached&quot; the 276.46 meter ship which arrived from the United Arab Emirates carrying 153,000 tonnes of crude oil for Bangladesh Petroleum Corporation on December 24.</p>
<p>They said the ship arrived 11 days behind schedule after its engine caught fire. The tanker had to be towed by a tug boat to Chittagong port.</p>
</text>
